Let $\Gamma$ be a $(d-1)$-dimensional simplicial complex on vertex set $\{1,\dots,n\}$, and let $I_\Gamma \subset S=\mathbb{K}[x_1,\dots,x_n]$ (with $\mathbb{K}$ an infinite field of characteristic $0$) be its Stanley–Reisner ideal. Let $\Theta=(\theta_1,\dots,\theta_d)$ be a generic linear system of parameters for $S/I_\Gamma$ and let $w$ be a generic linear form. One says that the Artinian reduction $A(\Gamma):=S/(I_\Gamma+(\Theta))$ has the almost strong Lefschetz property if, for every $k\le (d-1)/2$:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] the multiplication map $\cdot w^{\,d-2k-1}: A(\Gamma)_k \to A(\Gamma)_{d-1-k}$ is injective;
\item[(ii)] the multiplication map $\cdot w^{\,d-2k-1}: A(\Gamma)_{k+1} \to A(\Gamma)_{d-k}$ is surjective.
\end{itemize}
It is known that barycentric subdivisions of shellable (more generally, suitable) simplicial complexes satisfy properties (i) and (ii).

Problem: Exhibit, or classify, further classes of simplicial complexes $\Gamma$ (different from barycentric subdivisions) whose Stanley–Reisner Artinian reductions $S/(I_\Gamma+(\Theta))$ satisfy the almost strong Lefschetz conditions (i) and (ii) above.

